        "original_id": "899b89d2-b53e-5f73-924a-34dac75544a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Russell, Jerry Harrison, Tony Bongiovi, Lance Quinn\n- Bands/Songs/Works: Hecuba, \"Wild Combination\", \"Psycho Killer\"\n- Places: Los Angeles\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Russell, born Charles Arthur Russell Jr., was born on May 21, 1951, and died on April 4, 1992.\n- Arthur Russell was an American cellist, composer, producer, singer, and musician whose work spanned many styles.\n- In 1992, Jerry Harrison wrote in the liner notes for \"Psycho Killer\" that the single's b-side was an acoustic version featuring Arthur Russell on cello.\n- In those liner notes, Jerry Harrison said he was glad Tony Bongiovi and Lance Quinn were persuaded that the version with cellos should not be the only one.\n- Hecuba performed in Los Angeles at the premiere of \"Wild Combination,\" a film about Arthur Russell.\n- At the Los Angeles premiere of \"Wild Combination,\" Hecuba performed their versions of Arthur Russell's music.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
